<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 16th century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 1500s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/16th-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 1550 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 10088 5310" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 1550 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="5709" cy="970" r="172"/><text x="5709" y="1042" font-size="206">1</text></g><g><circle cx="4910" cy="989" r="172"/><text x="4910" y="1061" font-size="206">2</text></g><g><circle cx="7643" cy="1242" r="172"/><text x="7643" y="1314" font-size="206">3</text></g><g><circle cx="7018" cy="1385" r="172"/><text x="7018" y="1457" font-size="206">4</text></g><g><circle cx="4999" cy="1829" r="172"/><text x="4999" y="1901" font-size="206">5</text></g><g><circle cx="7088" cy="1864" r="172"/><text x="7088" y="1936" font-size="206">6</text></g><g><circle cx="5330" cy="692" r="172"/><text x="5330" y="764" font-size="206">7</text></g><g><circle cx="6029" cy="1964" r="172"/><text x="6029" y="2036" font-size="206">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 1550 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Kingdom of Bohemia &middot; Vijayanagara Empire &middot; Ottoman Empire &middot; Ming Empire &middot; Spanish Empire &middot; Mughal Empire &middot; Songhai Empire &middot; Ethiopian Empire</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Alcácer Quibir</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Spanish Armada</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Lepanto</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Mohács</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Act of Abjuration</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Marignano</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Charles V, Holy Roman Emperor</li><li>Tokugawa Ieyasu</li><li>Martin Luther</li><li>Ivan IV of Russia</li><li>Hernán Cortés</li><li>Toyotomi Hideyoshi</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1483–1546</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1500–1558</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1530–1584</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1543–1616</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1485–1547</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1537–1598</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><p class="ws-how">These words appear in the entries of this century. Explain each one in your own words.</p><ul class="ws-terms"><li><b>Bantustan</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Serfdom</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 1500s, 377 recorded states were founded and 298 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Ottoman Empire, the Spanish Empire and the Crown of Castile. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 16th century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/16th-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 16th century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Ottoman Empire <span>1299 CE – 1922 CE</span></li><li>Spanish Empire <span>1492 CE – 1898 CE</span></li><li>Ming Empire <span>1368 CE – 1644 CE</span></li><li>Mughal Empire <span>1526 CE – 1857 CE</span></li><li>Songhai Empire <span>1430 CE – 1600 CE</span></li><li>Vijayanagara Empire <span>1336 CE – 1646 CE</span></li><li>Kingdom of Bohemia <span>1198 CE – 1918 CE</span></li><li>Ethiopian Empire <span>1270 CE – 1974 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Battle of Marignano <span>1515</span></li><li>Battle of Mohács <span>1526</span></li><li>Battle of Lepanto <span>1571</span></li><li>Battle of Alcácer Quibir <span>1578</span></li><li>Act of Abjuration <span>1581</span></li><li>Spanish Armada <span>1588</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Charles V, Holy Roman Emperor <span>2: 1500–1558</span></li><li>Tokugawa Ieyasu <span>4: 1543–1616</span></li><li>Martin Luther <span>1: 1483–1546</span></li><li>Ivan IV of Russia <span>3: 1530–1584</span></li><li>Hernán Cortés <span>5: 1485–1547</span></li><li>Toyotomi Hideyoshi <span>6: 1537–1598</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><dl class="ws-key-terms"><dt>Bantustan</dt><dd>A Bantustan, or homeland, was a territory set aside for Black South Africans of a particular ethnic group under apartheid.</dd><dt>Serfdom</dt><dd>Serfdom was a form of unfree labour in which peasants were bound to the land and owed labour or dues to a lord.</dd></dl></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
